  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::64386",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp25 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp26, all of which are part of the MMP family and are participated by Mmp25. This indicates that Marimastat may influence Mmp25 through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of MMPs. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent interaction, though the specific molecular mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple MMPs participating in the same pathway implies that Marimastat may act as a regulator of MMP activity, potentially through binding to these proteins and influencing their function. This relationship is supported by the observed participation of Mmp25 in the pathway, suggesting a possible dependency on MMPs for its biological effects.",
